  "executive_briefing": "The global tax landscape is characterized by the full operationalization of Pillar Two, cementing a 15% global minimum tax for MNEs and driving a wave of real-time digital reporting mandates, exemplified by Singapore's InvoiceNow. Concurrently, the volatility in international trade tariffs persists, influenced by geopolitical shifts and potential policy reversals, particularly concerning US trade stances. Domestic corporate tax rates, while influenced by the global minimum tax, are also subject to national strategies for FDI attraction, leading to notable divergence, especially within the ASEAN region. Businesses must maintain agility in compliance and embrace data-driven reporting to navigate these complex and dynamic fiscal and trade environments.",
